# Rule file authoring

When creating or editing files in `.cursor/rules/`:

1. Apply the **write-cursor-rules** skill (`.cursor/skills/write-cursor-rules/` or `~/.cursor/skills/write-cursor-rules/`).
2. Keep one concern per `.mdc` file; target under ~50 lines.
3. Frontmatter must include `description` and `alwaysApply`; add `globs` when not always-on.
4. Use kebab-case filenames; actionable body with concrete ❌/✅ examples when useful.
5. Run the skill's validation checklist before finishing.

Do not duplicate User Rules from Cursor settings into project rules.
